---
/* Rich body for the "Leading and managing a design system" case
   study. The shared [slug].astro template renders this when the
   slug matches; the default templated layout is bypassed. Layout
   primitives (.rwc-* classes, .case-img-ph, image lightbox)
   mirror the other custom-body case components so all three feel
   consistent. */
---

<div class="rwc-body">

  {/* ───────────────────── HERO / CONTEXT ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-hero" id="case-context">
    <div class="rwc-hero-left">
      <div class="case-cat">Case study · StreamYard Design System</div>
      <h1 class="case-title">Leading and managing a design system</h1>
      <p class="case-subtitle">
        Implemented and led a cross-functional design system team across 6
        teams for enhanced product quality, accessibility, and efficiency.
      </p>

      <div class="rwc-callout">
        <div class="rwc-callout-title">
          <span class="rwc-callout-star" aria-hidden="true">★</span>
          Core achievements
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Coordinated 6 product teams' engineers and designers to
            continuously contribute to a design system.
          </li>
          <li>
            Enabled improved product accessibility (WCAG AA), refined
            components' design, and laid the foundations for a dark mode
            (a top customer request).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rwc-hero-right">
      <div class="case-img-ph rwc-hero-img is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/hero.webp" alt="StreamYard design system planning overview" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── MY ROLE ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-role" id="case-role">
    <div class="rwc-role-left">
      <div class="eyebrow">My role</div>
      <h2 class="rwc-h2">Lead designer and design system manager</h2>

      <p>
        The design system project was driven by a design-focused strategy,
        led by myself and another designer. We managed the project,
        coordinating with engineers, project managers, and documenting
        components thoroughly. Collaboration and reviews ensured high
        standards and alignment with project goals, showcasing the impact
        of strategic design leadership. We created foundational design
        elements and tokens for consistency and a single source of truth
        across design and engineering.
      </p>

      <dl class="rwc-aside">
        <div>
          <dt>My responsibilities</dt>
          <dd>Lead designer, Design system manager, Co-project manager, Front-end code reviewer</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>The team</dt>
          <dd>2 design leads, 6 designers, 7 engineers (from 6 separate product teams), 1 engineering manager</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Duration</dt>
          <dd>10 months</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── THE CHALLENGE ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-challenge">
    <div class="eyebrow">The challenge</div>
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">
      Design deliverables and code built were different. In some cases,
      there were 5+ variations of a single component.
    </h2>

    <p>
      The design team at StreamYard encountered significant hurdles that
      prompted the development of a robust design system. A notable
      disparity between designs and their corresponding code resulted in
      inconsistencies that impacted the final product's cohesion and
      quality. All designers frequently found themselves redoing components
      due to discrepancies in dimensions, spacing, and other crucial
      elements. Similarly, developers often had to reconstruct or adjust
      existing components, adding to their workload and impeding efficiency.
    </p>

    <p>
      Complicating matters was the product's extensive scale, which was
      already firmly established and operational in the market when the
      need for a formal design approach arose. This meant there was no
      existing infrastructure in Figma, forcing the team to construct
      everything from scratch. Furthermore, the design team operated at
      full capacity, with limited resources and no budget for expansion,
      posing challenges in resource allocation for this extensive endeavor.
    </p>

    <p>
      The adoption of a design system was viewed as a strategic maneuver to
      tackle these issues. By centralizing design components and
      establishing a singular point of truth through the design system, the
      team aimed to eradicate disparities and streamline both the design
      and development processes. Despite requiring a coordinated effort to
      do this, the objective was to build the system efficiently and
      strategically, ensuring it could address the challenges of aligning
      design with code, minimizing repetitive tasks, and bolstering overall
      product coherence without requiring team expansion. This wasn't
      merely a quick fix but a long-term investment in enhancing the
      quality and scalability of StreamYard's product design.
    </p>

    <div class="rwc-columns cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3>Engineers and designers were unhappy with the disparity between the design files and our Storybook library. It led us to severe inefficiency.</h3>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>By auditing component usage we identified the scale of the problem.</h3>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── ORGANIZING THE TEAM ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-organizing">
    <div class="eyebrow">Organizing the team</div>
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">
      We started by setting goals and our contribution model
    </h2>

    <p>
      To guarantee all team members had clarity on what to do, when, and
      why, we started by drafting OKRs for both design contributors and
      design system engineers. Design contributor goals were aimed at
      completing documentation for component proposals and building
      toolkits to increase design efficiency while ensuring great quality,
      whereas design system engineer goals targeted component merges and
      adoption over time in our codebases. We organized our process by
      setting up a contribution model detailing the required checkpoints
      each step of the way, starting from the ideation phase all the way
      to the adoption phase.
    </p>

    <div class="rwc-options">
      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/team-goals.webp" alt="Team Goals (Q1) in Notion — Build lovable products objective and key results" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <p class="rwc-caption">
          "Build lovable products" objective and key results, with 2 key
          results. Tracked weekly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-10">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/contribution-model.webp" alt="v2 - Contribution model flow diagram from Figma" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <p class="rwc-caption">
          Led a series of workshops aimed at agreeing on a contribution
          model for the design system, which became an integral part of
          each component's documentation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      The design system project was driven by a design-focused strategy,
      highlighting design's pivotal role in shaping project outcomes and
      product improvements. As design leads, we created core design
      elements and tokens for consistency across design and development.
      Using Figma and atomic design principles, we ensured components were
      adaptable and reusable. Acting as project managers, we collaborated
      closely with engineers, documenting components thoroughly for
      seamless handover. Continuous teamwork and reviews maintained high
      standards, showcasing the power of design leadership in tech
      development.
    </p>

    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/component-checklist.webp" alt="Figma Buttons component page with contribution-model checklist embedded in documentation" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="case-img-caption">
        Our contribution model then became a core part of our component
        documentation, where each designer had checkpoints for their
        component and guideline proposals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── ESTABLISHING WEEKLY PRACTICE ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-weekly-practice">
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">Establishing a weekly practice</h2>

    <p>
      As co-design lead and project manager at StreamYard, I orchestrated
      collaboration across 6 teams, guiding the project alongside another
      design lead. We coordinated design and engineering efforts,
      establishing foundational tokens and applying atomic design
      principles to create detailed components and guidelines. Our
      engineering team then transformed these into reusable React
      components, benefiting all of StreamYard's development and design
      teams.
    </p>

    <p>
      To keep all team members focused on our goal, I hosted a weekly
      design system sync to track progress week-in, week-out. Facilitating
      regular meetings among design and engineering leads ensured clear
      communication and alignment, preempting issues and maintaining
      momentum.
    </p>

    <p>
      My role was crucial in ensuring the design system met technical and
      aesthetic standards, enhancing workflow and product consistency.
    </p>

    <div class="rwc-options">
      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/cycle.webp" alt="Four-step design system cycle: Define experience specs, Build and adopt, Adopt and promote, Communicate and evolve" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-option">
        <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
          <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/slack-sync.webp" alt="DS Leads sync — Slack notes and takeaways from a weekly meeting" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/progress-board.webp" alt="SY Design System Jira board — components in To Do, In Progress, Ready to Publish, Published, and In Adoption columns" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="case-img-caption">
        Each week, we looked back at how we were doing to achieve our
        goals. Component adoption was tracked alongside design and
        engineering work, so progress stayed visible across both crafts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/quarter-status.webp" alt="This quarter status — 8 components to finalize design, 3 to adopt, plus building and adoption lists" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="case-img-caption">
        A quarter-at-a-glance view kept leadership and contributors aligned
        on what was finishing, what was building, and what was ready to
        adopt.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── DESIGN ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-design">
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">Design</h2>

    <p>
      Components were specified with the full surface area engineers needed
      to implement them: every type, variant, size, state, icon
      configuration, spacing token, and usage guideline. Each spec was
      paired with a contribution checklist so component handover stayed
      consistent across designers.
    </p>

    <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="16-9">
      <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/button-spec.webp" alt="Button component specification — spacing rules and usage guidance, light and dark variants side-by-side" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <p class="case-img-caption">
      The tokens and scoped variables allowed the entire theme to be
      swappable between light and dark modes with a simple setting change.
    </p>

    <div class="rwc-subsection">
      <div class="case-img-ph is-filled" data-ratio="4-3">
        <img src="/assets/images/cases/sy-ds/color-tokens.webp" alt="Color token table in Figma — neutral, primary, status with mapped light and dark values" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ───────────────────── OUTCOMES & IMPACT ───────────────────── */}
  <section class="rwc-section" id="case-impact">
    <h2 class="rwc-h2">Outcomes and impact</h2>

    <div class="rwc-stats">
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">6</div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Product teams united into a single DS team and roadmap.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">15<span class="rwc-stat-unit">+</span></div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Components designed and documented.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rwc-stat">
        <div class="rwc-stat-n">3</div>
        <div class="rwc-stat-desc">
          Core product improvements: WCAG AA*, Dark mode (upcoming),
          Design-to-code sync*. <em>* partial.</em>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      Despite the premature halt of the StreamYard design system project
      due to our parent company's sale, its initial progress significantly
      improved product consistency, aesthetics, and usability. Even
      incomplete, it streamlined workflows for both design and front-end
      development, reducing redundancy and effort. Despite constraints,
      our small team achieved remarkable progress in a short time,
      demonstrating dedication and skill. The partial rollout lays a
      foundation for future potential under new ownership.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>

{/* ───────────────────── IMAGE LIGHTBOX ─────────────────────
   Click-to-zoom for every <img> inside the case body. Single
   overlay element + delegated handler so it picks up any future
   images automatically. */}
<div class="rwc-lightbox" id="ldsLightbox" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Image preview" hidden>
  <button class="rwc-lightbox-close" type="button" aria-label="Close image preview">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
      <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/>
    </svg>
  </button>
  <img class="rwc-lightbox-img" alt="" />
</div>

<style>
  /* ===== Shared placeholder styling ===== */
  .case-img-ph {
    border: 2px dashed var(--border-emphasized, var(--border-subtle));
    border-radius: var(--dimension-radius-lg, 12px);
    background: var(--surface-muted, rgba(0,0,0,0.03));
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--dimension-space-24);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    min-height: 180px;
  }
  .case-img-ph[data-ratio="16-9"]  { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
  .case-img-ph[data-ratio="16-10"] { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }
  .case-img-ph[data-ratio="4-3"]   { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .case-img-ph.is-filled {
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: var(--surface-muted, rgba(0,0,0,0.04));
  }
  .case-img-ph.is-filled img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    border-radius: inherit;
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }
  .case-img-caption {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-align: right;
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-48);
  }

  /* ===== Body wrapper ===== */
  .rwc-body { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .rwc-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--font-line-height-loose);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-16);
  }
  .rwc-body h2.rwc-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-black);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    letter-spacing: var(--font-letter-spacing-tighter);
    line-height: var(--font-line-height-heading);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-20);
  }
  .rwc-body h3,
  .rwc-body h3.rwc-h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-32);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12);
  }
  .rwc-body .eyebrow { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12); }
  .rwc-caption {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm) !important;
    color: var(--text-tertiary) !important;
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-12);
  }

  .rwc-section {
    padding-top: var(--dimension-space-48);
    padding-bottom: var(--dimension-space-48);
    border-top: var(--dimension-border-width-1) solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .rwc-subsection { margin-top: var(--dimension-space-40); }

  /* ===== Hero ===== */
  .rwc-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--dimension-space-48);
    padding-bottom: var(--dimension-space-48);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-16);
    border-bottom: var(--dimension-border-width-1) solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .rwc-hero-img { min-height: 320px; }

  .rwc-callout {
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-24);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-primary) 16%, var(--surface-default));
    border: var(--dimension-border-width-1) solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--dimension-radius-lg, 12px);
    padding: var(--dimension-space-20) var(--dimension-space-24);
  }
  .rwc-callout-title {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--dimension-space-8);
  }
  .rwc-callout-star { color: #e6b800; }
  .rwc-callout ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .rwc-callout li {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--font-line-height-loose);
    padding-left: var(--dimension-space-16);
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-6);
  }
  .rwc-callout li::before {
    content: '•';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-brand);
  }

  /* ===== Role ===== */
  .rwc-role {
    padding-top: var(--dimension-space-48);
    padding-bottom: var(--dimension-space-48);
  }
  .rwc-aside { margin-top: var(--dimension-space-24); display: grid; gap: var(--dimension-space-16); max-width: 720px; }
  .rwc-aside dt {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--font-letter-spacing-wider);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-4);
  }
  .rwc-aside dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* ===== Multi-column blocks ===== */
  .rwc-columns {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--dimension-space-32);
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-24);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-32);
  }
  .rwc-columns.cols-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .rwc-columns h3 {
    margin-top: 0 !important;
    font-size: var(--font-size-base) !important;
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold) !important;
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-10) !important;
  }

  /* ===== 2-col option compare ===== */
  .rwc-options {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--dimension-space-32);
    margin-top: var(--dimension-space-24);
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-32);
  }
  .rwc-option h3 { margin-top: var(--dimension-space-20) !important; margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12) !important; }

  /* ===== Stats ===== */
  .rwc-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--dimension-space-40);
    margin: var(--dimension-space-32) 0;
  }
  .rwc-stat-n {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-black);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.6rem);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: var(--font-letter-spacing-tighter);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: var(--dimension-space-12);
  }
  .rwc-stat-unit {
    font-size: 0.6em;
    margin-left: 2px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .rwc-stat-desc {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    line-height: var(--font-line-height-loose);
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .rwc-stat-desc em { font-style: italic; opacity: 0.75; }

  /* ===== Responsive ===== */
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .rwc-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rwc-columns.cols-2,
    .rwc-options { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rwc-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--dimension-space-24); }
  }

  /* ===== Lightbox ===== */
  .rwc-body img:not(.rwc-lightbox-img) { cursor: zoom-in; }

  .rwc-lightbox {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1000;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--dimension-space-24);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity var(--motion-duration-standard, 220ms) var(--motion-easing-standard, ease);
  }
  .rwc-lightbox[hidden] { display: none; }
  .rwc-lightbox.is-open { opacity: 1; }

  .rwc-lightbox-img {
    max-width: 95vw;
    max-height: 95vh;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border-radius: var(--dimension-radius-md, 8px);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 64px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    cursor: zoom-out;
  }

  .rwc-lightbox-close {
    position: fixed;
    top: var(--dimension-space-20);
    right: var(--dimension-space-20);
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    color: #fff;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0;
    transition: background var(--motion-duration-short, 140ms) ease, transform var(--motion-duration-short, 140ms) ease;
  }
  .rwc-lightbox-close:hover,
  .rwc-lightbox-close:focus-visible { background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85); transform: scale(1.06); }
  .rwc-lightbox-close svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  /* Lightbox wiring — same pattern as the other case bodies.
     Own overlay id (ldsLightbox) keeps the three case studies'
     overlays from colliding if multiple ever co-existed on a
     page (they don't today, but cheap insurance). */
  (function () {
    function init() {
      var body = document.querySelector('.rwc-body');
      var overlay = document.getElementById('ldsLightbox');
      if (!body || !overlay) return;
      if (overlay.dataset.lbReady === '1') return;
      overlay.dataset.lbReady = '1';

      var lbImg = overlay.querySelector('.rwc-lightbox-img');
      var closeBtn = overlay.querySelector('.rwc-lightbox-close');
      var lastFocus = null;

      function openLb(src, alt) {
        lastFocus = document.activeElement;
        lbImg.src = src;
        lbImg.alt = alt || '';
        overlay.hidden = false;
        void overlay.offsetWidth;
        overlay.classList.add('is-open');
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        closeBtn.focus();
      }

      function closeLb() {
        overlay.classList.remove('is-open');
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = '';
        setTimeout(function () {
          overlay.hidden = true;
          lbImg.src = '';
          if (lastFocus && typeof lastFocus.focus === 'function') lastFocus.focus();
        }, 220);
      }

      body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var t = e.target;
        if (!t || t.tagName !== 'IMG') return;
        if (t.classList && t.classList.contains('rwc-lightbox-img')) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        openLb(t.currentSrc || t.src, t.alt);
      });

      overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        if (e.target.closest('.rwc-lightbox-close')) { closeLb(); return; }
        if (e.target === overlay || e.target === lbImg) closeLb();
      });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key === 'Escape' && !overlay.hidden) closeLb();
      });
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }
  })();
</script>
